---
error[E0819]: `o.inner.x` runs through `inner`, a field of the packed struct `Out`, so it cannot be lent
  --> mem:///main.lu:23:14
   |
23 |     bump(mut o.inner.x)
   |              ^^^^^^^^^ a `mut` claim lends its address
   |
   = note: `Out` is `#[repr(c, packed)]`: its fields sit at any byte offset, so a field's address
     need not be aligned for its type ([abi.layout.packed]). A packed field may be read and
     written; to lend one, copy it into a local, lend the local, and write it back.

